WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
The One Piece Manga just confirmed&nbsp;
that Shanks is on Elbaf getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.280
ready to fight Eustass Kid and taking his&nbsp;
road poneglyph. This is a major reveal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.800
that has incredible implications about Shanks’&nbsp;
true power, his real goal and how the Elbaf arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.540
will play out once the straw hats inevitably&nbsp;
get there after escaping from Egghead Island.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.280
Starting with the imminent battle between the&nbsp;
red hair pirates and the Kid Pirates. Does Kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.200
stand any chance at all against Shanks? And&nbsp;
what does this fight mean for the endgame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.480
of One Piece? Eiichiro Oda, the author of one&nbsp;
piece, has created 2 groups for the final Saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.060
that are competing for the One Piece treasure. And&nbsp;
interestingly enough, Luffy is part of both. On&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:44.220
the one hand you have the four Yonko, the most&nbsp;
powerful pirates in the world, Luffy, Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.660
Blackbeard and Buggy, but technically Mihawk.&nbsp;
And on the other hand the top fighters of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:54.900
worst generation, which are again Luffy, Kid and&nbsp;
Law. Which means that we have a total of 6 crews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.540
trying to get their hands on all 4 road poneglyphs&nbsp;
and reaching Laugh Tale first. And Oda has now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.580
put 2 of the Yonko up against two of the worst&nbsp;
generation. Law has been attacked by Blackbeard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.020
while Kid has actively sought out Shanks.&nbsp;
Blackbeard and Shanks want to get their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.430
hands on Kaido’s road poneglyph, while Law&nbsp;
would get the one Aokiji stole from Whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.140
Cake island. And Kid is trying to get the one&nbsp;
that is most likely hidden on Elbaf, protected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.180
by Jaguar D. Saul, the man with the burning&nbsp;
marks, who most likely rescued it from Ohara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.280
together with the rest of its ancient treasures.&nbsp;
This might actually the road poneglyph that went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.780
missing from fishman island, where Shanks saw&nbsp;
it when he was still part of Roger’s crew.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.400
Now we can not forget that both Kid and Law&nbsp;
have fought against Kaido and that both of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.020
them together have defeated Big mom. However,&nbsp;
it would truly take a small miracle for either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:48.720
of them to actually win a 1 vs 1 battle against&nbsp;
another Yonko, so shortly after leaving Wano.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.640
Especially since both Shanks and Blackbeard&nbsp;
have been heavily foreshadowed as two of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.020
main opponents that Luffy has to defeat&nbsp;
at some point in the story. Then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:04.200
who knows what sort of curve balls Oda has&nbsp;
planned for this final saga. And it also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:10.200
opens up the possibility that Luffy will run into&nbsp;
Buggy, Crocodile and Mihawk soon as well. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.660
I think it’s fair to say that Luffy has his&nbsp;
hands full right now. There is an Admiral and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:22.800
one of the Gorosei themselves coming for him with&nbsp;
an armada of 100 marine warships. And we actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.620
do not know yet, if Mihawk and Crocodile&nbsp;
actually want to compete for the One Piece.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.200
So let’s focus on the battle between kid and&nbsp;
shanks. When you put both characters next to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.480
each other like this, you will notice that they&nbsp;
share a lot of physical similarities. Both have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.880
red hair. Both have a scar over their left eye&nbsp;
and both are missing an arm. That last one is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.380
especially ironic, because Kid lost that arm in&nbsp;
his first encounter with the red hair pirates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:55.140
It turns out however, that it wasn’t Shanks&nbsp;
who cut it off. In fact Kid never even got to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:01.200
see Shanks during that fight. Instead, it seems&nbsp;
like Ben Beckman was the one who took Kid’s arm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:07.260
which kinda makes it look like some sort&nbsp;
of really morbid joke. Maybe Beckman saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:12.300
Kid and how similar he looked to Shanks and&nbsp;
thought to himself: You know what would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.620
hilarious..? I think we’re all about to&nbsp;
find out why the red hair pirates are all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:22.140
considered monsters and not just the group of&nbsp;
chill partying men that we have seen so far.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:28.200
While for the longest time it seemed like shanks&nbsp;
was the only yonko with only a small crew and no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:34.560
territory, this has been completely busted by&nbsp;
Oda at this point. We learned that Shanks has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.660
actually his own part of the new world that&nbsp;
he rules over and as Kid arrives at Elbaf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.680
we also get confirmation that&nbsp;
Shanks has a giant army of other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.820
pirate crews fighting for him, just&nbsp;
like Whitebeard, Big mom or Kaido.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:54.060
What is maybe the craziest part about this fight,&nbsp;
is it’s now 100% confirmed that Shanks wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.440
reach Laugh Tale himself. he did say, that&nbsp;
he wanted to enter the race when he appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.780
during Wano. However there was still a chance,&nbsp;
that he simply meant actively helping Luffy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.340
become pirate king. But in that case, Shanks&nbsp;
wouldn’t need Kaido’s road poneglyph. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:13.680
all Luffy already has that one. Which means&nbsp;
that he wants it for himself. This makes his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.140
true motivations even more mysterious than they&nbsp;
already were. After all, he could have taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.780
the Poneglyph from Luffy when he came to Wano.&nbsp;
Actually, Luffy would probably have just given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:30.180
it to him. Instead he just apparently just&nbsp;
came to save Luffy and co from Greenbull.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.420
So let’s put Kid aside here for a second and&nbsp;
talk about what it means that Shanks is in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.940
bar here on Elbaf with Dorry and Broggy. And&nbsp;
first of all, given that most theories that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:47.040
any of us make don’t end up coming true, it&nbsp;
feels nice being right for a change. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.780
I have been speculating about Shanks being the&nbsp;
secret protector of Elbaf for almost 4 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:55.500
now. In case you wonder what the hints&nbsp;
were for this, here’s a quick overview:

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.720
Elbaf, which is just the word fable spelled&nbsp;
backwards by the way, is the country of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:06.000
giants which has a giant tree in the middle&nbsp;
of it. While Wano was inspired by samurai and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:11.940
japanese mythology, Elbaf is clearly based on&nbsp;
Vikings and Nordic mythology. It’s a reference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:17.280
to the world tree Yggdrasil and the 7 realms,&nbsp;
one of which is the realm of giants and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:24.120
ruler is literally called Loki. The island was&nbsp;
first mentioned back in chapter 115 when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.980
straw hats ran into Dorry and Broggy, the two&nbsp;
giant warrior captains that are with Shanks in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:34.140
the bar here. Both of them wore Viking armour&nbsp;
and the ship of their giant pirate crew was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.580
also a classic viking ship. And you might not&nbsp;
know this, but one major inspiration for One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.620
PIece was actually the anime Vicky the Viking,&nbsp;
which was produced in both Germany and Japan.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:49.680
And you might or might not have noticed, that&nbsp;
Shanks himself actually has a really strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.680 --> 00:06:16.140
viking theme going on as well, that connected him&nbsp;
to Elbaf pretty much from chapter 1 in the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.940
First of all, Shanks’ ship is exactly the same&nbsp;
Viking design as the ships from Elbaf. Not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:03.420
that but Shanks is also inspired by the nordic&nbsp;
god Tyr. Now Tyr might not be as famous as Thor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:09.000
Odin or Loki, but he is actually one of the most&nbsp;
powerful and important gods in nordic mythology.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:14.460
He was apparently the god concerned with&nbsp;**the&nbsp;
formalities of war—especially treaties—and also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:21.060
appropriately, of justice.** Which of course fits&nbsp;
perfectly with Shanks’ role in the story so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:24.180
stopping the war at marineford&nbsp;
and all. On top of that though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:29.700
Tyr is most famous for sacrificing his arm to&nbsp;
the giant monster fenrir so that the other gods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:34.020
could bind him. Which of course is pretty&nbsp;
much in your face considering that shanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:39.540
also literally sacrifices his arm to a giant&nbsp;
monster in the first chapter of one piece.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:46.380
One thing, that is still unclear though, even&nbsp;
after chapter 1076, is whether Shanks is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:53.700
an ally and guardian of Elbaf, or if Elbaf is&nbsp;
actually under his rule and part of his territory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:59.520
An argument against Shanks being the ruler of&nbsp;
Elbaf is the existence of Loki and that big mom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:05.160
was confident that she could get the warriors of&nbsp;
ELbaf, known as the strongest army in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:10.860
on her side by marrying off Lola to&nbsp;
Loki. If Shanks acutally rules Elbaf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:16.680
that shouldn’t have been possible. At the&nbsp;
same time, one woman says to shanks that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:21.660
they should be paying protection money to&nbsp;
him for keeping them safe, kind of implying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:28.680
that Shanks has control over the island, kind&nbsp;
of like the yakuza in Japan. Dorry and Broggy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:34.800
also not only refer to Shanks as big brother,&nbsp;
which also sounds like respectful yakuza lingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:39.840
but they also willingly follow Shanks into&nbsp;
battle, even though they both are captains.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.720
Which of course leaves a very&nbsp;
important question on the table:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.020
If Shanks is allied with the&nbsp;
giants of Elbaf right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:53.040
how will Usopp be able to lead them at the end&nbsp;
of the story? Something that has been majorly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.040 --> 00:09:01.080
foreshadowed. Let’s look at what Shanks being on&nbsp;
Elbaf means for the Elbaf arc and the straw hats.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:07.440
And first of all, if it wasn’t already obvious&nbsp;
that Luffy and Co will be going to Elbaf soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:13.380
Shanks being there is the ultimate proof that&nbsp;
it will happen. Just think of all the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:18.720
arcs that are leading to this island. There is the&nbsp;
adam tree, that produces the indestructible wood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:23.400
that the thousand sunny is made out of. It is also&nbsp;
most likely the main entrance to the sky islands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:29.760
and Birka, which would make it the perfect arc to&nbsp;
introduce Urouge, the one supernove we have seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:34.380
no trace of so far. Of course we have also just&nbsp;
learned that the entire knowledge of the library&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:40.920
of Ohara has been transported safely to Elbaf&nbsp;
by Saul, making a reunion with Robin a must-see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:46.020
Then there is this color spread of the straw&nbsp;
hats as vikings. And let’s be real, if Oda had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:51.540
planned to skip going to Elbaf altogether, he&nbsp;
surely would have shown it off to us in all its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:57.480
glory instead of shrouding it in so much mystery&nbsp;
and barely giving us a glimpse of its shoreline.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:04.260
but the two most important character arcs i want&nbsp;
to see on Elbaf are of course Luffy and Usopp.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.700
Especially now that the red hair pirates are&nbsp;
confirmed to be there. You have of course Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:13.380
overdue meeting with Shanks to prove himself&nbsp;
as a great pirate. But before we get into that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:19.140
I want to talk about Usopp first, because&nbsp;
I’m convinced that Elbaf will be his arc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.760
As you might know Usopp has gained the respect&nbsp;
of various Elbaf giants throughout the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:31.020
including Dorry, Broggy, Oimo, Kashi and Hajrudin.&nbsp;
Usopp is inspired by the giants of Elbaf to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:36.660
a brave warrior of the sea. As Usopp’s lies&nbsp;
keep coming true, Usopp could really become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:43.560
the leader of the giants and lead an army of 8000&nbsp;
men into battle beside Luffy, like he once said.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:48.660
Also remember, that we have the mysterious&nbsp;
prince Loki. In nordic mythology, Loki is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:54.240
known to be a trickster an liar. But so is&nbsp;
Usopp. Both of them might be quite similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:58.860
in terms of their personality, but while Usopp&nbsp;
values bravery and wants to be like the giants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:05.160
Loki mostly values himself and oppresses the&nbsp;
other giants. So Usopp could show his bravery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.920
by challenging Loki to a duel. Now we have the&nbsp;
classic theme of David with his slingshot vs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:17.400
the giant Goliath. At this point it would also be&nbsp;
a waste, if Oda didn't give Usopp a Mjolnir-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:22.980
hammer, to parallel Thor and Loki. And who knows,&nbsp;
maybe another lie will come true and Usopp might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:28.740
awaken his conquerors haki after Luffy and Zoro,&nbsp;
something fans have been speculating for a while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:34.080
now. And on top of all that, we have of course&nbsp;
the entire relationship with his father Yasopp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:39.120
the sniper of Shanks’ crew. In a way he is&nbsp;
responsible for Usopp being a coward and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:45.000
liar in the first place. When he left Usopp and&nbsp;
his mother, he left Usopp with 2 choices: Resent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:50.700
his father for leaving or, as he did in the end,&nbsp;
glorifying him. After all why would he leave his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:56.580
only kid behind, if he wasn't a legendary pirate&nbsp;
with very important work to do? This really hits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.580 --> 00:12:02.040
home hard, when you realize that it's probably&nbsp;
EACTLY THIS insecurity about being left behind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:08.160
that lead to Usopp's chronic lying. He lies about&nbsp;
being a great and powerful man, having had many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:13.740
adventures, just like his father, because he&nbsp;
feels like he could never truly BE this person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:20.160
in reality. He sees himself as weak, insecure and&nbsp;
worthless. So confronting his father and finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:26.040
closure could truly be the breakthrough for Usopp,&nbsp;
that makes him one of the most badass Straw Hats.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:31.980
But the biggest thing about Elbaf will of&nbsp;
course be Luffy finally meeting Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.360
getting the chance to prove himself to his&nbsp;
mentor. And here it will be really interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:42.840
to see what Shanks’ true intentions are. Is he&nbsp;
good, neutral or maybe even the secret villain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:48.360
of the story? To find out what will most likely&nbsp;
happen when Luffy arrives at Elbaf to meet Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:53.400
you can watch this video right here with all the&nbsp;
evidence in the story so far. Shanks for watching.

